# Resolution
Fixed by the observability-formatting hardening work shipped in:

- `7085c81` `Harden trace formatting for request metadata`
- `8d37645` `Harden observability debug formatting`
- `aeb1180` `Complete observability formatting hardening`

The resolution keeps AWS-compatible key semantics unchanged and instead makes
observability output safe.

Implemented changes:

- `crates/observability/src/lib.rs` now provides shared escaped and redacted
  formatting helpers for tracing and debug output
- attacker-controlled identifier types in `crates/storage/src/types.rs`,
  including `ObjectKey`, now implement observability-safe `Debug`
- high-risk trace sites in `crates/server-core/src/coordinator.rs`,
  `crates/server-http/src/http/mod.rs`, `crates/server-http/src/http/serve.rs`,
  `crates/storage/src/node.rs`, and `crates/storage/src/pg_store.rs` now use
  escaped `{:?}` formatting or explicit observability helpers instead of raw
  `{}` formatting
- remaining high-risk HTTP traces also avoid raw path and `Range` formatting

Ongoing guidance for future code lives in `guides/observability-formatting.md`.
